---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import PlaceholderBox from "../components/PlaceholderBox.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import Disclaimer from "../components/Disclaimer.astro";
import { href } from "../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Models & data"
  description="Model card for the two supplied models: inputs, labels, preprocessing, data, limits, and parity status. No measured figures for the demo models yet."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Models & data"
    intro="Model card for the two supplied models only. No measured figures for these two models are published. Reported project results live on the Research page and do not describe these files."
  />
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Models in scope</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>File (as supplied)</th><th>Output</th><th>Labels file</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Stage 1 — gate</td>
            <td><code>keras_model.h5</code></td>
            <td>2 classes</td>
            <td><code>labels.txt</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Stage 2 — health</td>
            <td><code>keras_model (1).h5</code></td>
            <td>4 classes</td>
            <td><code>labels (1).txt.txt</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Header inspection (read-only, files unmodified) confirms: Keras format, a MobileNet-style
      backbone, input 224 by 224 by 3, and output counts matching the labels files (2 and 4). The
      models are never retrained, modified, or replaced. Conversion for the browser is the only
      permitted change, and only with a passing parity test.
    </p>
    <p>
      No counting model was supplied. No model files, weights, or converted models are published on
      this site. Ownership and licensing are unconfirmed; see the FAQ.
    </p>

    <h2>Labels (exact)</h2>
    <p>Stage 1: <code>0 Honey Bee or Beehive</code>; <code>1 Not Honey Bee or Not Beehive</code>.</p>
    <p>
      Stage 2: <code>0 Healthy Honey Bee or Healthy Beehive</code>;
      <code>1 Deformed Wing Virus (DWV)</code>;
      <code>2 Varroa Mite Infestation</code>;
      <code>3 Chalkbrood Disease</code>.
    </p>
    <p>Stage 2 runs only when the Stage 1 label starts with "0". This gate comes from the working inference code, not from the report.</p>

    <h2>Preprocessing (demo)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Convert to RGB, centre-crop to a square and resize to 224 by 224 (Lanczos resampling).</li>
      <li>Scale pixel values to the range minus 1 to 1 (divide by 127.5, subtract 1).</li>
      <li>Run Stage 1. If the label starts with "0", run Stage 2 on the same prepared image.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small muted">
      The report describes different training preprocessing (a 0 to 1 range with aspect-preserving
      padding, §4.3). That description does not apply to the demo. The inference code above is
      authoritative for the demo, and the parity test checks it.
    </p>

    <h2>Measured performance</h2>
    <PlaceholderBox text="measured results on a labelled parity set supplied by the team — test-set size, per-class results, and parity report link. Nothing is published until measured." />
    <p><StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Parity set pending" /> <StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Parity report pending" /></p>
    <p>Why report figures are not attached to these two models:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The report's Chapters 4, 5, 11, and 12 give different metric sets that disagree on every disease class.</li>
      <li>Three report values also appear in the literature review as other researchers' results. They are withheld everywhere on this site until the project lead confirms in writing that each was independently measured in this project and on which test set.</li>
      <li>No report metric is tied to the two supplied model files by name. The report never mentions the model files, the labels files, or the inference code.</li>
      <li>Chapter 12 reassigns Chapter 5 numbers to different tasks, and one chapter mentions a fifth disease category that is never named.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Reported project results are published, with exact sources, on the
      <a href={href("/research")}>Research</a> page. They describe the project as reported — not
      these two files. Publishing any report figure as if it described these files would mislead
      readers. Measured figures only, after the parity run.
    </p>

    <h2>Training data as described in the report</h2>
    <p>Per model, with section citations. These describe the report's datasets. They are not verified as the training data for the supplied files.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Binary classifier: over 50,000 images (35,000 bee images, 15,000 others), split for training and checking, with augmentation (§4.4).</li>
      <li>YOLO-based bee counting (research): 10,000 manually annotated hive images with over 20,000 bee boxes (§4.6). No counting model is supplied here.</li>
      <li>Disease testing set in Chapter 11: over 5,000 labelled images across the four labels, with part held out for testing (§11.4.1).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Sources named in the report (Chapter 9): public datasets, web-collected material, and field
      photos and videos from unnamed apiaries. No dataset names, links, or licences are given.
      Licences and consent are therefore recorded as unknown. No training images are republished
      here.
    </p>

    <h2>Intended use and limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Intended use: decision support for beekeepers and inspectors, from close, well-lit photos. Not a diagnosis.</li>
      <li>Visual-only checking cannot spot early or internal disease with no visible sign (report §6.3.1).</li>
      <li>Poor photos (blur, darkness, distance) give unreliable results. The report's own checks were weakest on subtle and early-stage cases (§11.8).</li>
      <li>Testing in the report stayed mainly in controlled settings (§6.5.1). Behaviour across seasons, regions, and bee species is not established here.</li>
      <li>Out of scope: Nosema, foulbrood, queen status, colony strength, and any treatment advice.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Conversion and parity status</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Conversion scripts and run instructions: ready, in the repository <code>ml/</code> folder.</li>
      <li>Browser conversion: not yet run (needs a TensorFlow environment; see the Colab runbook).</li>
      <li>Parity test set: 30+ licensed images collected for backend-agreement testing (labels unverified, so no accuracy claim can come from them). A labelled set from the team or experts is still needed for measured accuracy.</li>
      <li>Parity report: pending. If parity fails, the demo switches to a Python API instead of changing the models.</li>
    </ul>

    <Disclaimer />
    <p><a href={href("/detector")}>Detector pipeline</a> · <a href={href("/learn")}>Learn the labels</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
